Description: QuartzFire geolocation (country) traffic filtering
 Country-based allow/block filtering for QuartzFire (VyOS-based NGFW),
 equivalent to WatchGuard Fireware's Geolocation service. Uses the IPFire
 libloc location database (signed, free to redistribute — deliberately NOT
 MaxMind GeoLite2) and enforces with per-country nftables sets in a dedicated
 table, one set lookup per new connection.
 .
 A single Rust multi-call binary (qzgeo) provides the `service geolocation`
 conf-mode owner, the standalone resync, the signed database updater
 (wrapping the vendor `location update` tool, hence the dependency), the
 IP-lookup diagnostic, and the status/counters plumbing the QuartzFire WebUI
 reads. Links libloc directly for database queries.
